      "body": "## Motivation\n\nA batch that mixes requests with and without images is rejected in two places:\n\n- **`/generate` and the Engine API.** `GenerateReqInput._normalize_image_data` decides whether `image_data` holds one image list per request by looking only at `image_data[0]`. If the first request has no image, as in `[None, [\"a.png\"]]`, the batch is read as a flat list and every entry is wrapped again (`[[None], [[\"a.png\"]]]`). The request then fails with `Invalid image: [...]`. The same batch in the other order, `[[\"a.png\"], None]`, already works.\n- **`/vertex_generate`.** The route collects `image_data` only from the instances that have one. `[{\"text\": \"a\", \"image_data\": \"u\"}, {\"text\": \"b\"}]` therefore sends `[\"u\"]` for a batch of two and fails with `The length of image_data should be equal to the batch size.` Any Vertex batch that mixes image and text-only instances is rejected.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `GenerateReqInput._normalize_image_data` treats `image_data` as one list per request when any entry is a list, not only the first one.\n- `vertex_generate` sends one entry per instance: either `None`, or that instance's images as a list (a single image is wrapped). When no instance has images, `image_data` stays `None` as before.\n- Regression tests:\n  - `test_first_request_without_images` in `test_io_struct.py`.\n  - `TestVertexGenerateRoute` in `test_generate_api_contract.py`, which drives the route with a fake tokenizer manager that runs the real normalization.\n\nThe open #41768 also edits `io_struct.py`, but changes `_handle_parallel_sampling`; the two do not overlap.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A for model outputs, since only request normalization changes.\n\nEnd-to-end check on one RTX 4090 with `Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct`. The server was the v0.5.21 image with this patch applied; both changed functions are identical in v0.5.21 and main. Each batch element was compared with the same request sent alone at temperature 0.\n\n| Request | Batch | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `/generate` | `[None, [img]]` | 400 `Invalid image` | matches |\n| `/generate` | `[None, [img, img]]` | 400 `Invalid image` | matches |\n| `/vertex_generate` | image instance, then text instance | 400 length mismatch | matches |\n| `/vertex_generate` | text instance, then image instance | 400 length mismatch | matches |\n\nBatches that already worked still match: `[img, None]`, `[None, img]`, `[[img], None]`, `[[], [img]]`, `[[img], [img, img]]`, `[img, img]`, and two image instances on Vertex.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. This changes request normalization only.\n\n## Tests\n\n- On main, `test_first_request_without_images` and all three subtests of `TestVertexGenerateRoute` fail. With this change they pass.\n- `test_io_struct.py` and `test_generate_api_contract.py`: 71 passed.\n- `test_mm_hashes.py` and `test_serving_chat.py`: 166 passed.\n- pre-commit passes on the changed files.\n\nCommand run from `test/`:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=../python python -m pytest \\\n  registered/unit/managers/test_io_struct.py \\\n  registered/unit/entrypoints/test_generate_api_contract.py\n```\n\nThe tests ran on commit `5d8c43bde3`, based on main at `4560da58ee`. The environment was the `lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-20261014-684fea8a` image (Python 3.12.15, PyTorch 2.14.1+cu130, Transformers 5.19.0). These are CPU unit tests.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format the changed code with the repository's pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] Add regression tests to the existing CPU-registered test files.\n- [ ] Update documentation (not applicable).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmarks (not applicable; see the end-to-end check above).\n- [x] Follow the repository's code style guidelines.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38684442859](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38684442859)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38684442947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38684442947)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38684442927](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38684442927)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
